WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
Your cells run a web of linked reactions.

2
00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.150
Almost every step has its own enzyme.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.840
That adds up to thousands
of different enzymes,

4
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.770
each one a protein.

5
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.190
Each one speeds up its
reaction, then leaves unchanged,

6
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.660
ready to go again.

7
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.580
So how can a protein make a
reaction millions of times faster,

8
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.860
yet come out of it unchanged?

9
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.930
In this mission, you'll
read an energy diagram:

10
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.230
where a reaction starts, where
it ends, and the climb between.

11
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.300
Then you'll zoom in on the active site:
a small pocket whose shape and charges

12
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.130
suit one substrate.

13
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.200
Your mission: find out how a protein can
speed up a reaction millions of times,

14
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.920
yet come out unchanged.
